      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "If you can get 10 avatars on screen with high poly counts in a quest world like the home world or hub, reaching 72fps with smooth frame times, then I would believe you. Until then these restrictions are necessary on both platforms.\n\nVR software does a lot to compensate for low frame rates and the quest is no exception. Everything my appear smooth but you would not be hitting a high enough frame rate for the optimal experience and the frame timings would be resulting in an unstable frame rate or stutter.\n\nIn addition to all this, even if the poly count did perform well, developing an app for the oculus quest has some recommendations and guidelines that vrchat are keeping as close to as they can.",
      "viewerReactions": null
    },
